<title>TURKEY: Turkish Tofas Q1 profits fall 65.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Turkish Tofas Q1 profits fall 65.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-March 1997 provisional</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)    38.12 vs     193.24</p>
<p>    Net profit		    320.19 vs     927.57</p>
<p>    Net sales		  16,560.04 vs  13,967.26</p>
<p>    Operating loss		391.98 vs   1,136.06 profit</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	2,665.23 vs   1,008.00</p>
<p>    Interest paid		 482.19 vs     750.49</p>
<p>    Extraordinary expense   1,219.09 vs	20.68</p>
<p>    Total debts		18,517.09 vs  13,972.44</p>
<p>    Equity		     25,483.91 vs  17,918.80</p>
<p>    Capital		     8,400.00 vs   4,800.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Turkey's leading car maker Tofas Turk Otomobil Fabrikasi A.S. is equally owned by Koc conglomerate and Italy's Fiat Auto. Each partner has a 37.86 percent stake.</p>
<p>The company plans to raise capital to 12.6 trillion lira by issuing 0.5 bonus for one existing share and pay out a 143 lira cash dividend per 1,000 lira nominal-valued share from 1996 profits from May 30.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 77 percent annual wholesale in March.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875</p>
</text>
